<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Frozen feed for builds up to 1.0.2, which carry the old bundle identifier
  com.dogukyilmaz.Battistics.

  Sparkle refuses to install an update whose bundle identifier differs from
  the running app's (Autoupdate/AppInstaller.m compares the two and fails),
  so those builds cannot be updated in place at all. An item with no
  <enclosure> is an informational update: Sparkle shows the notice and sends
  the user to <link> instead of downloading anything.

  Attach this file as appcast.xml on every release. Old copies poll
  releases/latest/download/appcast.xml, so it has to keep resolving. Newer
  builds read appcast-2.xml and never see this.

  The link points straight at the 1.1.0 DMG rather than the releases page,
  so Sparkle's "Learn More" starts the download instead of opening a page to
  hunt through. It is pinned to 1.1.0 on purpose: any build with the new
  identifier can update itself the ordinary way afterwards, so this only has
  to carry someone across the identifier change once. Do not delete the
  v1.1.0 release while this is live.
-->
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:sparkle="http://www.andymatuschak.org/xml-namespaces/sparkle">
  <channel>
    <title>Battistics</title>
    <link>https://github.com/doguyilmaz/battistics</link>
    <description>Battery statistics for the Mac.</description>
    <language>en</language>
    <item>
      <title>Battistics has moved — one manual update needed</title>
      <link>https://github.com/doguyilmaz/battistics/releases/download/v1.1.0/Battistics-1.1.0.dmg</link>
      <sparkle:version>1.1.0</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <h2>Download this one by hand</h2>
        <p>A newer Battistics corrects a misspelling in the app's internal
        identifier. macOS treats the result as a different app, so it cannot
        install itself over the copy you are running.</p>
        <p>Click <b>Learn More</b> to download it, then drag the new
        Battistics to your Applications folder, replacing the old one. Your
        charge and health history is kept. Menu bar and notification settings
        reset to their defaults, and macOS asks about notifications once
        more.</p>
        <p>Automatic updates resume normally afterwards.</p>
      ]]></description>
    </item>
  </channel>
</rss>
